{
  "name": "Download Instagram & Facebook Videos/Reels with Telegram Bot",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Instagram & Facebook Video Downloader Bot\n\nSend a public Instagram Reel or Facebook video link to your Telegram bot. It replies with the video and the creator, caption, and hashtags, saves the file to Google Drive, and logs it to a content library sheet.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Telegram Trigger** receives each message sent to the bot.\n2. **Extract Link** finds the first Instagram or Facebook link in the message text or caption.\n3. Messages without a supported link get a help reply. Supported links get a \"Downloading…\" reply.\n4. **Get Post Details** reads the post's creator, caption, and hashtags from its link preview.\n5. **Route by Platform** looks up the video file through a downloader service for that platform.\n6. **Download Video** downloads the file. It's uploaded to Google Drive and logged to the content library, then **Send Video** replies with it.\n7. If a step fails, the bot replies with an error. Videos Telegram won't accept (bots can upload up to 50 MB) are sent as a Drive link instead.\n\n### Setup\n- [ ] Create a bot with @BotFather and add its token as a Telegram credential on the trigger and every Telegram node\n- [ ] **Upload to Google Drive**: connect Google Drive and choose the folder for downloads\n- [ ] **Log to Content Library**: connect Google Sheets and select an empty sheet. Columns are created automatically.\n- [ ] Activate the workflow and send the bot a link\n\n### Download services\nVideo links come from third-party downloader sites: snapdownloader.com for Instagram and fbdownloader.to for Facebook. These sites can change or go offline without notice. If one platform stops working, replace its **Fetch** and **Find** nodes.",
        "height": 1040,
        "width": 640,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "57177adf-1f58-4bcf-8063-3a554d4e8121",
      "name": "Sticky Note6",
